1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,940
Disease costs humanity three hundred ninety-seven point four trillion dollars annually.

2
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:09,880
That's more than global G.D.P. (one hundred and one trillion dollars).

3
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:18,180
The number sounds wrong because economists spent centuries measuring productivity without accounting for the people who

4
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:28,060
stopped being productive on account of being dead. The missing piece is disability-adjusted life years, or D.A.L.Y.s: healthy

5
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:33,760
years deleted by disease. Die at 40 instead of 80? That's 40 D.A.L.Y.s.

6
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:44,440
Spend 10 years severely depressed? That's 5 D.A.L.Y.s. Globally: 2.55 billion D.A.L.Y.s annually.

7
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:52,160
At three times G.D.P. per capita (one hundred fifty thousand dollars per year), that's three hundred eighty-two point five

8
00:00:52,160 --> 00:01:00,240
trillion dollars in lost human potential, plus eight point two trillion dollars in direct medical costs and six point seven

9
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:08,020
trillion dollars in lost productivity. That's the bill. Here's the receipt for the fix: Your D.F.D.A.

10
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:13,120
(a decentralized F.D.A.) costs forty million dollars per year to run.

11
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:18,620
It saves fifty-eight point six billion dollars per year in clinical trial waste.

12
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:23,000
That's six hundred thirty-seven to one returns on R. and D.

13
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:31,500
savings alone. Total societal benefit (including lives saved): eighty-four point eight million to one.

14
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:34,660
I know. Those numbers look like someone fell asleep on the keyboard.

15
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:41,960
They didn't. Here's the breakdown. The Math: From forty-one thousand dollars to five hundred dollars.

16
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:47,620
Traditional Phase Three trials cost forty-one thousand dollars per patient.

17
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:55,220
That's a Tesla. Per person. To find out if a pill works. The pill costs 37 cents to make.

18
00:01:55,780 --> 00:02:03,340
The paperwork weighs more than the patient. Then the Oxford RECOVERY trial proved you can do the same thing for five hundred

19
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:11,920
dollars. During a pandemic. While panicking. They tested COVID treatments on forty thousand plus patients by: Using existing

20
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:16,740
hospital staff (revolutionary concept: doctors treating patients).

21
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:21,920
Collecting data electronically (instead of sacrificing forests to the paperwork gods).

22
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:26,320
Focusing on what actually matters: does the patient live or die?

23
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:31,820
(not "did they complete form 27-B in triplicate?"). Your D.F.D.A.

24
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:36,440
takes this model global. eighty to one hundred sixty times cost reduction.

25
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:45,120
Same data quality. Better real-world applicability. It turns out you don't need 17 committees to answer the question "did

26
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:49,780
the medicine work?". Where the fifty-eight point six billion dollars Comes From.

27
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:58,160
Global clinical trial spending: sixty billion dollars per year (and growing, because apparently inefficiency scales beautifully).

28
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:05,940
Baseline estimate: ninety-seven point seven percent efficiency gains across the market (based on RECOVERY trial's actual

29
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:14,360
per-patient cost ratio). Ninety-seven point seven percent of sixty billion dollars equals fifty-eight point six billion

30
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:19,800
dollars saved annually. What fifty-eight point six billion dollars Buys You.

31
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:26,620
Each new drug approval is worth an average of one point six two billion dollars in market value.

32
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:34,960
The F.D.A. approves roughly fifty drugs per year per year. That is the speed at which a species with nuclear weapons and

33
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:39,400
artificial intelligence has chosen to cure itself. Staggering.

34
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:46,060
With twelve point three times more trial capacity, you could test far more treatments at once.

35
00:03:46,820 --> 00:03:54,480
With the money saved every year, you could: Fund ten thousand new pragmatic clinical trials (at five million dollars each,

36
00:03:55,060 --> 00:04:03,100
which is still luxurious by RECOVERY standards). Test treatments for seven thousand rare diseases currently ignored (because

37
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:07,560
orphan diseases aren't profitable enough for your orphan-making economic system).

38
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:16,040
Cut drug development time from seventeen years to three to five years (most terminal patients don't have seventeen years;

39
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:23,900
this has not occurred to anyone in charge). Make medicines affordable by eliminating two point six billion dollars in development

40
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:28,580
costs (roughly ninety percent of which is lawyers arguing about commas).

41
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:37,720
Daily Opportunity Cost. Every day without this system costs one hundred sixty-one million dollars in wasted trial spending

42
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:47,220
alone. Delayed treatments cost seven point nine four billion disability-adjusted life years, or D.A.L.Y.s, each year.

43
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:53,190
All because of the regulatory lag period. The lag period is not a safety feature.

44
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:58,340
It is a waiting room where people die. You just gave the waiting room a nicer name.

45
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:04,800
See Daily Opportunity Cost of Inaction for calculations. What It Costs to Run.

46
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:10,270
Your D.F.D.A. costs forty million dollars a year to operate.

47
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:16,040
Servers, engineers, compliance, global integration. The boring stuff that saves billions.

48
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:24,260
One-time build cost is similar. For context, this is roughly what your species spends annually on Halloween costumes for

49
00:05:24,260 --> 00:05:29,520
dogs. I need you to sit with that for a moment. Less than one fighter jet.

50
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:33,660
Less than one yacht. Less than what FIFA spends on "hospitality."

51
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:40,140
See D.F.D.A. Cost-Benefit Analysis for detailed costs. R.O.I.

52
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:49,530
Scenarios. In the conservative scenario, the R.O.I. is six hundred thirty-seven to one, counting R and D savings only (N.P.V.

53
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:58,440
over ten years). In the recommended scenario, the R.O.I. is eighty-four point eight million to one, counting R and D savings

54
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:05,000
plus post-safety efficacy lag elimination. In the worst case scenario, the R.O.I.

55
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:09,000
is sixty-six to one, based on higher costs and lower adoption.

56
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:16,800
Even the worst case (everything goes wrong, adoption is terrible, the engineers quit and the servers catch fire) returns

57
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:22,220
sixty-six to one. That beats every military investment in human history.

58
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:27,300
Your worst medical outcome is still better than your best military one.

59
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:31,000
Let that sink in while you're approving next year's defense budget.
